### Scheduled Scaling Policy

A scheduled scaling policy adjusts the capacity of an auto-scaling group based on a predetermined schedule, such as time of day or day of the week.

Example scheduled scaling policy:

```yaml
{
  "Type": "ScheduledAction",
  "Recurrence": "0 9 * * MON-FRI",
  "MinSize": 5,
  "MaxSize": 10,
  "DesiredCapacity": 8
}
```

In this example, the auto-scaling group will scale to a minimum of 5 instances, a maximum of 10 instances, and a desired capacity of 8 instances every weekday at

